---
description: Consistent native property editor widths and alignment
alwaysApply: true
---

When changing UI in this repository, follow `docs/UI_LAYOUT.md`.

- Preserve fonts, colors, bindings, native control behavior and the existing Gurux.DLMS package.
- Standard property sections use EditorLayoutPolicy: 800 logical pixels maximum, 144-pixel label rail (minimum 100), 640-pixel field/action-group maximum.
- Align peer input edges. Wrap and measure captions. Use current-DPI constants, never cumulative font/size scaling.
- Keep tables, charts, lists and structured/multiline data flexible. Document compact compound and external-provider exceptions.
- Example: PPP Setup and MAC Address Setup use the same bounded scalar rows; a profile data table may expand across the window.
- Render every affected screen at normal/narrow/restored sizes with empty and populated content. Inspect screenshots and record actual monitor coverage.
- Preserve the dashboard's existing independent layout and autosave decisions.
